module

public import Sheaf.Algebra.Lie.KostantIntegralPBW
import Sheaf.Algebra.Lie.SplitSemisimpleRootDecomposition
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.RootSystem.BaseExists

/-!
# Simple divided powers generate the positive integral Kostant form

Source: Mathieu, Tilting Modules and their Applications (2000), Section 1, pp. 150–151;
Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Theorem 23.71, pp. 508–509, and Appendix C.21–C.22, p. 612.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-positive-kostant-simple-divided-generation)

Both forms use the existing `LieAlgebra.kostantIntegralForm`, restricted to the positive
roots and the simple roots respectively. All generation and linear combinations are over
`ℤ` inside the rational universal enveloping algebra, before any change of scalars.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u v

namespace LieAlgebra

/-- The positive integral Kostant form equals the integer algebra generated by the simple
positive divided powers. Equivalently, each positive divided power is a finite integer
linear combination of words in those generators. Empty root systems give the bottom unital
integer subalgebra, namely the image of `ℤ`, on both sides.

Source: Mathieu, Section 1, pp. 150–151, simple-divided-power integral-form convention;
Milne, Theorem 23.71, pp. 508–509, and Appendix C.21–C.22, p. 612, for the normalization
and root chains used in the following argument.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-positive-kostant-simple-divided-generation)

Proof plan:
1. Let S be the unital integer algebra generated by the simple divided powers. Induct
   strongly on the exponent n, and inside that induction on positive-root height. For n = 0
   the generator is one; simple roots belong to S for all exponents by construction.
2. The split root decomposition and lem-sfb-root-base-rational-integral-spans identify
   the based reduced crystallographic root pairing. Apply
   lem-sfb-positive-root-simple-chain to a nonsimple positive root gamma, writing its last
   step as gamma = c + a with a simple and c positive. Reducedness makes a and c independent:
   otherwise c = a and gamma = 2a would be a root. Let p be maximal with c - p a a root,
   put b = c - p a, and k = p + 1. By lem-sfb-root-string-integer-interval, b - a is not
   a root. A positive simple coordinate outside a persists in b, so sign coherence makes
   b positive, and its height is strictly smaller than gamma's. Now gamma = b + k a.
3. Apply lem-sfb-root-string-divided-adjoint-triangular to a, b, k and n. Each term of
   the alternating divided-adjoint sum belongs to S: the a factors are simple and the
   b factor uses the inner induction. Every correction monomial has all exponents below
   n, so the outer induction puts it in S. Subtraction gives epsilon^n e_gamma^(n) in S;
   epsilon is a sign, so multiplication by the same sign gives e_gamma^(n) in S. This
   closes both inductions without dividing by any root-string constant.
4. Every positive generator therefore belongs to S. The reverse inclusion holds because
   every simple root is positive, giving equality. The integer span of finite words
   contains one as the empty word and is closed under sums, negatives and products by
   distributivity; it is exactly S, giving the finite-sum assertion. If the root index
   type is empty, both generating sets are empty and both adjoins are the scalar image. -/
theorem positive_kostantIntegralForm_eq_simple
    (L : Type u) [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra ℚ L] [FiniteDimensional ℚ L]
    [HasTrivialRadical ℚ L] (H : LieSubalgebra ℚ L) [IsLieAbelian H]
    (hmax : ∀ K : LieSubalgebra ℚ L, H ≤ K → IsLieAbelian K → K = H)
    (I : Type v) [Finite I] (P : RootPairing I ℚ (Module.Dual ℚ H) H)
    [P.IsRootSystem] [P.IsCrystallographic] [P.IsReduced]
    (heval : ∀ (a : Module.Dual ℚ H) (h : H), P.toLinearMap a h = a h)
    (Δ : P.Base) (e : I → L)
    (he : ∀ i : I, e i ∈ LieModule.weightSpace L (P.root i) ∧ e i ≠ 0)
    (hopp : ∀ i : I, ⁅e i, e (P.reflectionPerm i i)⁆ = (P.coroot i : L))
    (hadd : ∀ i j k : I, P.root i + P.root j = P.root k →
      ∃ ε : ℤ, (ε = 1 ∨ ε = -1) ∧
        ⁅e i, e j⁆ = ((ε : ℚ) * (P.chainBotCoeff i j + 1)) • e k)
    (hzero : ∀ i j : I, P.root i + P.root j ∉ Set.range P.root →
      P.root i + P.root j ≠ 0 → ⁅e i, e j⁆ = 0)
    (B : Module.Basis (Δ.support ⊕ I) ℚ L)
    (Bh : ∀ i : Δ.support, B (Sum.inl i) = (P.coroot i.val : L))
    (Be : ∀ i : I, B (Sum.inr i) = e i) :
    (kostantIntegralForm (fun i : {i : I // Δ.IsPos i} ↦ e i.val) =
      kostantIntegralForm (fun i : Δ.support ↦ e i.val)) ∧
    (∀ (i : I), Δ.IsPos i → ∀ n : ℕ,
      ∃ (t : ℕ) (c : Fin t → ℤ) (w : Fin t → List (Δ.support × ℕ)),
        Algebra.rationalDividedPower (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι ℚ (e i)) n =
          ∑ j : Fin t, c j • ((w j).map (fun d ↦
            Algebra.rationalDividedPower (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι ℚ (e d.1.val))
              d.2)).prod) ∧
    (IsEmpty I →
      kostantIntegralForm (fun i : {i : I // Δ.IsPos i} ↦ e i.val) = ⊥ ∧
      kostantIntegralForm (fun i : Δ.support ↦ e i.val) = ⊥) := by
  sorry

end LieAlgebra
